- op: discuss  # 076c
  at: '2026-09-10T12:27:35Z'  # 076c
  by: agent  # 076c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 076c
  clock: 4  # 076c
  nonce: 076c  # 076c
  message: "CLOSED ON THE FILED ROW; THE RESIDUAL IS WI-gokop. Shipped in PR #892 (merged,\ndev 1847d60400). This item's own stated closure criterion was \"the hinted share\nmust move on corpus, measured the same way\" — it moved, on both repos, and the\npart that did NOT move is a different mechanism now carried by its own item.\n(`pending_validation` is invariant-only; this is a work_item, so `done` with the\nresidual filed is the available shape. The awaits_bakeoff_validation discipline\napplies to WI-gokop and to this PR's quantitative claims.)\n\nMEASURED, baselines re-derived on this tree rather than quoted (the denominator\nmoved since filing: sbt 10,985 -> 16,018). Record:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pokam_scala_09102026/RESULT.md; FIX_PLAN.md was\npre-registered before any corpus number existed.\n\n  repo   hinted share             module-slot share\n  sbt    9.03% -> 23.43% (+14.4pp)   4.63% -> 18.19% (+13.6pp)\n  lila   4.50% ->  8.02% (+3.5pp)    0.89% ->  3.99% (+3.1pp)\n\n`calls_total` IDENTICAL in both repos (sbt 30,132, lila 68,853) — nothing lost;\nthe edges that left the unresolved population became RESOLVED project bindings.\n\nTHE FILING NAMED ONE SHAPE; THERE WERE THREE, and they are one bug. The\ninline-qualified annotation miss reproduced, but `new java.io.File(\"p\")` loses\nthe hint identically — and this item lists `val x = new Foo()` among the shapes\nthat WORK, so a fix scoped to the annotation branch would have left it broken\nAND LOOKED LIKE A FIX. A GENERIC APPLIED type (`Buffer[String]`) is not in the\nfiling at all. Four sites that each looked for the bare node themselves now\nshare one walk (INV-motos).\n\n**THE MEASUREMENT CHANGED THE CHANGE, AND THIS ITEM'S OWN METRIC WOULD HAVE\nPREFERRED THE WORSE VERSION.** The first cut scored 28.07% hinted on sbt.\nSampling what it newly RESOLVED found `.get` on a standard-library `Map[K,V]`\nbinding to the PROJECT's `Map.get` in sbt/SessionVar.scala; counted, 44 of 185\nnewly-resolved edges (24%) bound to an implicitly-imported name — the \"arbitrary\nsame-named internal def\" funnel scala.py refuses for untyped receivers. Denying\na generic base Scala imports implicitly drops the hinted share to 23.43% and\nRAISES the slot share (18.07 -> 18.19) with 0 mis-binds, because an unqualifiable\nname never filled a slot. A hint is necessary, not sufficient (L5).\n\nPRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION REFUTED: generics were to dominate qualified names on\nBOTH repos. sbt 2,180 vs 213; lila 284 vs 1,068 — the reverse. Opposite idioms,\nand a single-repo run would have \"confirmed\" whichever one I ran.\n\nWHAT REMAINS (WI-gokop): lila still sits at 8.02%, barely out of the 5-10% band\nthis item was filed on, and the rest is INFERENCE — a receiver bound from a call\nresult, a for-comprehension binder, a lambda parameter, a chained receiver. That\nneeds the return-type registry objc and swift already have, and WI-gokop carries\nboth the sizing instruction and the precision warning this PR earned."  # 076c
